134:Grounding: Material Design, "Movement" (deceleration on entry, acceleration on permanent exit, sharp on temporary exit, standard for on-screen and relative movement, with the 225/195/300 ms mobile durations); Thomas & Johnston, *The Illusion of Life* (1981), via Toon Boom's 12-principles summary (slow in / slow out = easing; anticipation = a preparatory move before a larger action; follow-through = parts settling after the main body stops); FrontendHelpers' cubic-bezier guide, citing Nielsen Norman Group (enter ease-out, exit ease-in and shorter, on-screen move ease-in-out, 100–400 ms for most UI motion; `y>1` = overshoot past the endpoint, `y<0` = anticipation pull-back). Full study: `hidden_files/archer-calendar/research/2026-11-14.md`.
